# Host minimums lea doctor checks (issue #108). Every lea container shares the host kernel, so the
# host's patch level is part of the containment.
#
# No Docker Engine minimum: Moby 29.4.2's seccomp fixes (AF_ALG and socketcall, CVE-2026-31431) are
# in Docker's default profile, which lea does not use; lea runs image/seccomp.json, which carries
# the same hardening. lea doctor shows the Docker Engine, containerd and runc versions.
#
# podman MIN: Podman 5.8.4 fixes CVE-2026-57231 (GHSA-4hq8-gpf5-8p68: an image's key-only ENV
# passes the host's variable of that name into the container). lea is built for Docker Engine:
# on a Podman host, below this minimum is a warning (lea doctor and the launcher), never a
# refusal; Podman's bridge has no gateway_mode_ipv4=isolated.
podman 5.8.4
#
# kernel ID VERSION_ID MIN: the oldest kernel release (uname -r, without its flavour suffix) of
# that distribution (/etc/os-release) that carries the fixes for CVE-2026-74753 (perf
# use-after-free), CVE-2026-80521 (af_unix SCM_RIGHTS race) and CVE-2026-80841. Add a line only
# once the distribution's changelog shows the three fixes, for example on Ubuntu:
#   apt changelog linux-image-$(uname -r) | grep -nE 'CVE-2026-(74753|80521|80841)'
# A distribution without a line gets a warning in lea doctor, never a failure.
#
# lox MIN: the oldest lox (lox version) lea starts the Lock Family hub with; lea runs
# `lox init` and `lox up`, which an older lox does not have.
lox 0.5.0
